-- title:
--   Serre's theorem A in Čech form over a base ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $r$ a natural number, and $P$ a scheme equipped with a closed immersion $\iota : P \to \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded ring of homogeneous polynomials in $r+1$ variables over $A$, together with a morphism $q : P \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ such that $\iota$ followed by the structure morphism $\mathbb{P}^r_A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ equals $q$. Let $F$ be a module datum over $q$: an assignment of an $A$-module and $\Gamma(P,U)$-module $F(U)$ to each open $U \subseteq P$, the two actions compatible, together with $A$-linear restriction maps semilinear over restriction of functions and functorial. Assume $F$ is coherent, i.e. $F(U)$ is a finite $\Gamma(P,U)$-module for every affine open $U$, and quasi-coherent, i.e. for every affine open $U$ and every $f \in \Gamma(P,U)$, each element of $F(D(f))$ becomes, after multiplication by some power of $f$, the restriction of an element of $F(U)$, and each element of $F(U)$ restricting to $0$ on $D(f)$ is annihilated by some power of $f$. Then there is $d_1 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for every $d \ge d_1$ there are $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ in the kernel of the Čech differential on $0$-cochains of the open-by-open tensor product $F \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} \iota^{*}\mathcal{O}(d)$ (the twist datum written in the standard frames) relative to the ordered affine cover of $P$ by the preimages $\iota^{-1}(D_+(x_j))$, $j = 0,\dots,r$, such that for each $0$-simplex $s$ of that cover the values $\sigma_l(s)$ generate $(F \otimes \iota^{*}\mathcal{O}(d))$ on the corresponding chart as a module over the ring of functions there.
--
--   This is Serre's theorem A — a coherent sheaf on a closed subscheme of $\mathbb{P}^r_A$ becomes generated by finitely many global sections after a sufficiently large twist — stated for coherent quasi-coherent module data and in Čech form on the pulled-back standard cover, with no Noetherian hypothesis on $A$. It is used to produce, for large $d$, a surjection from a finite free module datum onto the $d$-th twist of $F$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_OModulePresheaf_exists_forall_exists_H0_tensor_twist_span_eq_top.lean

